    <statement><p>The value of <m>\displaystyle \int_{5}^{9} \frac{1}{ x^2 } dx</m> is</p>
<p><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{-1}{9}+\frac{1}{5}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\displaystyle \int u^n du = \frac{u^{n+1}}{n+1}</m>:
<me>\parbox{0.4\textwidth}{

\ \begin{aligned}
\int_{5}^{9} \frac 1 {x^2} dx  \amp  = \int_{5}^{9} x^{-2} dx \\\\ 
\amp  =	\left (-1)x^{-1} \right|_{5}^{9} = \left \frac{-1}{x} \right|_{5}^{9}	\\\\
\amp  =	\frac{-1}{9} - \frac{-1}{5}	= \frac 1 {5} - \frac 1 {9} = 0.0888889
\end{aligned} }</me>



</solution>
